      "content": "Here's a concise summary and main themes for Heart of Darkness:\n\n\"Set in the Congo Free State during the late 19th century, Joseph Conrad's Heart of Darkness explores the darker aspects of human nature, colonialism, and the blurred lines between civilization and savagery. As Marlow's journey deep into the African jungle progresses, he confronts the darkness within himself and the brutal reality of colonialism, challenging the facade of Western superiority. Themes include the destructive effects of imperialism, the complexities of moral ambiguity, and the fragility of human values in the face of chaos.\"\n\nThis summary should fit well into your course description. Good luck with the syllabus!",
